THREE HELPERS C INLINES AND THE PORT CALLED OUT OF LINE — 17.7 M CALLS PER
512x512 PHOTO FRAME AT p2, ALL GONE, -290.6 M Ir (-0.63 %), byte-identical.
`MdRates::txt_rate` 5,974,663 calls, `tx_pipeline::rs_tx_size` 6,984,051 and
`coeff_c::tx_size_from_dims` 4,766,423 are all ZERO after this. Wall clock
1.012x on a photo at 512 p2 and 1.007-1.008x on the gradient at 256 / 512 p2.
**With the two commits before it, the photo's p2 port/C instruction ratio is
1.777 -> 1.694 and the whole-frame wall clock is 1.056x** (gradient 1.054x at
256 p2, 1.042x at 512 p2).

AND THE PART WORTH KEEPING: `#[inline]` ALONE FIXES ONE OF THE THREE. Measured
as its own step below — with the attribute and nothing else, `txt_rate` inlined
(5,974,663 -> 0) but `rs_tx_size` stayed at 6,984,051 calls and
`tx_size_from_dims` at 4,762,229, because LLVM will not inline a 19-arm
`match` on `(w, h)` that is called from several places, whatever the attribute
says. Turning both into a table index is what removed them.

