        --tool=callgrind (Ir only), rustc 1.98.1. GATES both hosts.
base2:  main@origin 2f59c2e0 (the residual-hoist commit) — the SOLO reference,
        built in a sibling directory whose only difference from `cand` is these
        five files.
base0:  main@origin 41e5d8f1 — before all three chunks; the cumulative reference.
cand:   this commit.
C:      reference/svt-av1 @ 3115c0c1, the PREBUILT oracle, NOT rebuilt.
tools:  tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh + callcount.py on the CID22 photo
        (sha256 88142a48...), presets 2 and 6, qp 40, STILL. Wall clock:
        tools/perf_ab.sh, 21 interleaved randomised-order paired rounds, one
        untimed warmup per sample, NEITHER SIDE NICED, box quiet. Memory:
        tools/mem_peak.sh.
data:   benchmarks/txsize_tables_2026-09-05.tsv.

=================== WHAT THESE THREE ARE ===================

`callcount_realimg_2026-09-04` item F: "OUT-OF-LINE HELPERS (port only, no C
symbol because C inlines them)" — `MdRates::txt_rate` 5,974,663 calls /
382.3 M Ir, `tx_pipeline::rs_tx_size` 6,984,051 / 167.4 M,
`coeff_c::tx_size_from_dims` 4,766,423 / 113.0 M at photo_cid p2, together
~1.4 % of the frame. That 1.4 % is INCLUSIVE Ir — it counts the work the
helpers actually do, and only the call frames and the branch chains are
removable. This chunk removes 290.6 M of it (0.63 %); the arithmetic that
remains is folded into the callers.

  * `MdRates::txt_rate` (rate_tables.rs) — C's `av1_txt_rate_est`
    (product_coding_loop.c:4711) is a static helper the compiler inlines into
    `tx_type_search`. `#[inline]` is all it needed.
  * `coeff_c::tx_size_from_dims` — a 19-arm `match (w, h)`, called once per
    `tx_unit_inner` (4,238,186 times) plus once per `txt_search` (496,519).
    Now a 5x5 table indexed by `(log2(w) - 2) * 5 + (log2(h) - 2)`, with a
    sentinel for the six illegal aspect ratios; two shifts and a load.
  * `tx_pipeline::rs_tx_size` — the SAME 19-way mapping again, into the port's
    own `TxSize` enum, called 6,984,051 times from `tx_unit_inner` (1.65 per
    invocation: once for the forward dispatch, once for the inverse) for a
    value the function was already holding as `c_tx`. Now `TX_SIZE_FROM_C[c_tx]`
    at those two sites — a const array of the 19 `TxSize`s in C's
    `TX_SIZES_ALL` order — and a table lookup at the remaining sites.

=================== BYTE IDENTITY, AND HOW THE TABLES ARE PINNED ===================

Both replaced `match`es are KEPT IN THE TREE, `#[cfg(test)]`, as
`tx_size_from_dims_match` and `rs_tx_size_match`, and two new tests assert the
table agrees with the match on EVERY power-of-two pair in 4..=64: it must
accept exactly the same 19 shapes (asserted by count, so a table typo that
silently accepts a 20th fails) and reject exactly the same six, plus a
non-power-of-two / out-of-range set. That is a stronger check than the encode
gates, because it covers the shapes a still-picture grid never codes.

  crates/svtav1-encoder/src/entropy/coeff_c.rs
      tx_size_table_tests::tx_size_table_matches_the_match_form
      tx_size_table_tests::tx_size_table_rejects_illegal_dims
  crates/svtav1-encoder/src/leaf_funnel/tests.rs
      rs_tx_size_table_matches_the_match_form

